			<item>
				<title>About This Site</title>
				<link>https://projektemacher.org/en/post/backsteinexpressionismus/about/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate><author>mail@christianmahnke.de (Christian Mahnke)</author>
				<guid>https://projektemacher.org/en/post/backsteinexpressionismus/about/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;Due to &lt;a href=&#34;https://projektemacher.org/post/fuenf-jahre-wesermuende&#34;&gt;some&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;https://projektemacher.org/post/das-paula-becker-modersohn-haus-in-bremen&#34;&gt;experiences&lt;/a&gt; in my childhood, buildings in a distinctive style caught my eye. For a long time without knowing exactly what it was about. From time to time I happened to think of it, e.g. in Hanover. Only when I was in Halle more often in 2014 and noticed some buildings there as well, I started to take a closer interest&amp;hellip;.&#xA;And so for several years I have put together a small collection of illustrations, mostly postcards or books. These are presented here.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Links</title>
				<link>https://projektemacher.org/en/post/backsteinexpressionismus/links/</link>
